rmgk_gekko: the size of a rollback state slot can be set at build time

GekkoNet allocates every state slot at the size it is given (prediction window + 2 slots and
one more), and RMG-K gives 24 MiB per slot: about 240 MB for a 7-frame window. The core's
rollback state is 8,438,120 bytes, so on the Switch that is mostly unused memory the console
does not have to spare. The size is local (GekkoNet never sends it), so it can differ between
the two players. Without RMGK_GEKKO_STATE_CAPACITY nothing changes: the Mac build keeps 24 MiB;
builder/build-switch.sh passes 10 MiB.

--- a/RMG-Core/rmgk_gekko.cpp
+++ b/RMG-Core/rmgk_gekko.cpp
@@ -70,7 +70,10 @@
 
 namespace
 {
-constexpr unsigned int kGekkoStateCapacity = 24u * 1024u * 1024u;
+#ifndef RMGK_GEKKO_STATE_CAPACITY
+#define RMGK_GEKKO_STATE_CAPACITY (24u * 1024u * 1024u)
+#endif
+constexpr unsigned int kGekkoStateCapacity = RMGK_GEKKO_STATE_CAPACITY;
 constexpr int kGekkoMaxLoggedFrames = 600;
 constexpr int kGekkoWaitSleepUs = 100;
 // Lobby matches leave player drops to the lobby (MATCH_PEER_LEFT). GekkoNet's
